 genistein administration</article-title><source><italic>Toxicological Sciences</italic></source><year>2006</year><volume>90</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>230</fpage><lpage>240</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16352619</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rimbach</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>De Pascual-Teresa</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ewins</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Antioxidant and free radical scavenging activity of isoflavone metabolites</article-title><source><italic>Xenobiotica</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>33</volume><issue>9</issue><fpage>913</fpage><lpage>925</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14514441</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kulling</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Honig</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Simat</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Metzler</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Oxidative in vitro metabolism of the soy phytoestrogens daidzein and genistein</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Agricultural and Food Chemistry</italic></source><year>2000</year><volume>48</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>4963</fpage><lpage>4972</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11052763</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fang</surname><given-names>Y-C</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>B-H</given-names></name><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>R-FS</given-names></name><name><surname>Lu</surname><given-names>Y-F</given-names></name></person-group><article-titl