lant extracts</article-title><source><italic>Methods in Enzymology</italic></source><year>2001</year><volume>335</volume><fpage>273</fpage><lpage>282</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11400376</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kisseleva</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Brenner</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hepatic stellate cells and the reversal of fibrosis</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Gastroenterology and Hepatology</italic></source><year>2006</year><volume>21</volume><issue>supplement</issue><issue>3</issue><fpage>S84</fpage><lpage>S87</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16958681</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bataller</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Brenner</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hepatic stellate cells as a target for the treatment of liver fibrosis</article-title><source><italic>Seminars in Liver Disease</italic></source><year>2001</year><volume>21</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>437</fpage><lpage>451</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11586471</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>X-J</given-names></name><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Mao</surname><given-names>Y-Q</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Effects of the tyrosine protein kinase inhibitor genistein on the proliferation, activation of cultured rat hepatic stellate cells</article-title><source><italic>World Journal of Gastroenterology</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>8</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>739</fpage><lpage>745</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12174389</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kang</surname><given-names>L-P</given-names></name><name><surname>Qi</surname><given-names>L-H</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>J-P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Effect of genistein and quercetin on proliferation, collagen synthesis, and type I procollagen mRNA levels of rat hepatic stellate cells</article-title><source><italic>Acta Pharmacologica Sinica</italic></source><year>2001</year><volume>22</volume><issue>9</issue><fpage>793</fpage><lpage>796</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11749858</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig position="float" id="F1"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Schematic design of study.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="MI2007-36381.001" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F2"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>(a) Control (group 1): normal liver histology (H&#x00026;E x200);(b) group 4: inflammation, necrosis was increased in group 4 (<chem-struct xlink:type="simple">CCl<sub>4</sub></chem-struct>)(H&#x00026;E x200); (c) group 5: inflammation and necrosis was decreased in group5 (<chem-struct xlink:type="simple">CCl<sub>4</sub></chem-struct> +genistein): (H&#x00026;E x200).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="MI2007-36381.002" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F3"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>(a) Group 4: actine expression was increased in group 4 (x400);(b) group5: actine expression was decreased in group 5 (x400).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="MI2007-36381.003" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Level of malondialdehyde (MDA) and gluathione, ALT, AST in groups.</